@page "/how-it-works"

<PageTitle>How BlokeBot works</PageTitle>

<article class="article-shell">
    <header class="article-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h1>Set up once, then run the channel from one dashboard</h1>
        <p class="lede">BlokeBot keeps each channel's connection, people and tools together without making everyday tasks feel technical.</p>
    </header>

    <ol class="process-list">
        <li>
            <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Choose the channel</h2>
                <p>Sign in, select the Twitch channel you own or help manage, and confirm its readiness.</p>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Connect and choose tools</h2>
                <p>Complete the connection action shown for the channel, then turn on commands, guessing or points independently.</p>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Prepare before going live</h2>
                <p>Set command replies, guessing answers, point rules or giveaway timings while the dashboard shows what still needs attention.</p>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Run and review</h2>
                <p>Use the live controls, let moderators help where permitted, and share read-only leaderboards with viewers.</p>
            </div>
        </li>
    </ol>

    <MediaFigure
        Source="/media/channel-setup.png"
        Alt="BlokeBot channel setup showing Twitch chat readiness, connection actions and bot status."
        Caption="Channel setup explains what is ready and the next action when something is missing." />

    <aside class="next-panel" aria-labelledby="how-next-heading">
        <h2 id="how-next-heading">Ready for the details?</h2>
        <p>The user guide follows the same tasks you see in the dashboard.</p>
        <p><a class="button button-primary" href="/guide/getting-started">Start the guide</a></p>
    </aside>
</article>
